# TorBox Abuse and Illegal Content Reporting Policy

Last updated: July 31, 2026

This Abuse and Illegal Content Reporting Policy (the “**Policy**”) explains how to report non-copyright abuse, illegal content, security abuse, and other misuse involving TorBox, TorBox.App, our websites, applications, dashboard, APIs, software, tools, bots, integrations, support services, and related products and services (collectively, the “**Service**”).

This Policy is intended for non-copyright abuse reports. Copyright notices must be submitted under the TorBox Copyright / DMCA Policy.

## 1. How to Report Abuse

Reports of non-copyright abuse, illegal content, malware, phishing, threats, child safety issues, non-consensual intimate imagery, privacy violations, account abuse, API abuse, payment abuse, or other misuse may be submitted to:

[abuse@torbox.app](mailto:abuse@torbox.app)

To help us review your report, please include enough information to identify the material, account, request, or activity at issue. Helpful information may include:

1. URLs, magnet links, torrent hashes, info hashes, file hashes, filenames, file sizes, NZB information, Usenet information, hoster links, RSS feed information, webhook information, or other technical identifiers;
2. the date and time of the activity, including your time zone;
3. account identifiers, request identifiers, API activity, screenshots, logs, or other information that may help us locate the issue;
4. a description of why you believe the material or activity violates the law, the TorBox Terms of Service, the Acceptable Use Policy, or another TorBox policy;
5. your name and contact information, unless you are submitting an anonymous report; and
6. any other information that may help us understand and evaluate the report.

Please do not include sensitive personal information unless it is necessary for us to review the report.

## 2. Copyright Complaints

Copyright complaints must be submitted under the TorBox Copyright / DMCA Policy. Copyright complaints sent to [abuse@torbox.app](mailto:abuse@torbox.app) may be redirected to the designated copyright agent or may not be processed unless they include the information required by the Copyright / DMCA Policy.

If your report involves copyright infringement, please use the DMCA process instead of this Policy.

## 3. Types of Abuse Covered by this Policy

This Policy may be used to report non-copyright issues involving the Service, including:

1. child sexual abuse material, child exploitation material, grooming, or sexualization of minors;
2. non-consensual intimate imagery, revenge pornography, sextortion, or image-based abuse;
3. malware, phishing, credential theft, botnets, exploit kits, ransomware, spyware, or other harmful code;
4. threats, harassment, stalking, doxing, extortion, impersonation, or fraud;
5. terrorism, violent extremism, credible threats of violence, or incitement to violence;
6. stolen credentials, stolen payment information, account takeover, identity theft, or payment fraud;
7. privacy violations, unlawful disclosure of personal information, or misuse of personal data;
8. illegal pornography, obscene material, or other unlawful sexual content;
9. sanctions evasion, money laundering, terrorist financing, export-control violations, or restricted-party transactions;
10. API abuse, bot abuse, webhook abuse, search/indexer abuse, RSS abuse, automation abuse, or integration abuse;
11. attempts to evade takedowns, de-caching, blocking, account restrictions, rate limits, payment obligations, or enforcement measures; and
12. any other use of the Service that may violate the TorBox Terms of Service, Acceptable Use Policy, this Policy, or applicable law.

## 4. Emergency Matters

If you believe there is an emergency involving imminent harm, credible threats, child exploitation, terrorism, violent activity, or another urgent safety issue, you should contact appropriate law enforcement or emergency authorities immediately.

You may also report the matter to TorBox at [abuse@torbox.app](mailto:abuse@torbox.app), but TorBox is not an emergency service and cannot guarantee immediate review or response.

## 5. Child Safety Reports

TorBox does not permit child sexual abuse material, child exploitation material, grooming, or sexualization of minors.

If TorBox identifies or receives a report involving suspected child sexual abuse material or child exploitation, TorBox may remove, block, de-cache, restrict, preserve, report, or disclose information to law enforcement, child safety organizations, service providers, or other appropriate parties, as permitted or required by law.

Do not submit, transmit, upload, forward, or attach child sexual abuse material when making a report. Instead, provide technical identifiers, URLs, hashes, account information, timestamps, screenshots that do not contain illegal imagery, or other information that may help us locate and evaluate the report.

## 6. Non-Consensual Intimate Imagery

TorBox does not permit use of the Service to access, request, download, cache, store, stream, export, seed, distribute, promote, or facilitate non-consensual intimate imagery, revenge pornography, sextortion material, or image-based abuse.

Reports involving non-consensual intimate imagery should include information sufficient to identify the material or activity at issue. TorBox may remove, block, de-cache, restrict, preserve, or take other action regarding reported material or associated accounts.

## 7. Malware, Phishing, and Security Abuse

TorBox does not permit use of the Service to create, access, request, download, cache, store, stream, export, transmit, distribute, or make available malware, phishing content, stolen credentials, botnet infrastructure, exploit kits, ransomware, spyware, credential stealers, or other harmful code or materials.

Reports involving malware, phishing, or security abuse should include technical indicators where available, such as URLs, hashes, filenames, IP addresses, request identifiers, API activity, screenshots, logs, timestamps, and a description of the suspected abuse.

## 8. API, Integration, Automation, and Indexer Abuse

TorBox does not permit use of APIs, bots, webhooks, RSS feeds, search/indexer configurations, metadata tools, automation features, or integrations to infringe rights, facilitate illegal activity, overload the Service, evade enforcement, or create discovery tools for infringing or illegal content.

TorBox may restrict, revoke, rotate, suspend, or disable API keys, access tokens, bots, webhooks, RSS feeds, integrations, automated tools, or accounts that TorBox believes are insecure, abusive, excessive, unlawful, harmful, unauthorized, or otherwise inconsistent with the Terms of Service, Acceptable Use Policy, or this Policy.

## 9. Review of Reports

TorBox may review abuse reports based on the information provided, legal requirements, technical feasibility, operational needs, user safety, service integrity, and applicable policies.

Submitting a report does not guarantee that TorBox will take the action requested. TorBox may decline to act on reports that are incomplete, inaccurate, abusive, fraudulent, duplicative, automated without proper review, submitted in bad faith, or unsupported by enough information to identify the material or activity at issue.

TorBox may also take action on reports that do not include every item requested in this Policy if TorBox can reasonably identify the material or activity at issue.

## 10. Actions TorBox May Take

TorBox may take any action it determines appropriate in response to suspected abuse, illegal content, security issues, fraud, rights violations, or misuse of the Service.

Actions may include:

1. blocking, removing, de-caching, disabling access to, or restricting materials, files, hashes, links, torrents, NZBs, hosters, sources, streams, exports, download requests, integrations, or other materials;
2. preventing re-adding, re-caching, or future matching requests for materials;
3. warning users;
4. throttling, rate-limiting, or restricting activity;
5. rotating, revoking, disabling, or restricting API keys, access tokens, webhooks, bots, RSS feeds, or integrations;
6. suspending, downgrading, restricting, or terminating accounts, plans, paid features, vouchers, or Service access;
7. preserving information;
8. reporting suspected illegal activity to law enforcement, regulators, child safety organizations, rights holders, payment processors, vendors, infrastructure providers, or other appropriate parties;
9. disclosing information as described in the Terms of Service, Privacy Policy, and applicable law; or
10. taking any other action TorBox determines necessary to protect the Service, users, third parties, vendors, payment processors, infrastructure providers, partners, or the public.

TorBox may take action with or without notice. TorBox is not required to provide prior notice if TorBox determines that immediate action is appropriate for legal, security, abuse, copyright, payment, operational, or risk-management reasons.

## 11. Preservation and Disclosure

TorBox may preserve, access, use, or disclose information associated with an account or use of the Service if TorBox believes doing so is required or permitted by law, necessary to respond to legal process or governmental requests, necessary to enforce the Terms of Service or TorBox policies, or necessary to protect TorBox, users, third parties, or the public.

TorBox may also preserve information related to abuse reports, legal requests, security incidents, fraud, payment disputes, repeat abuse, suspected illegal activity, or policy violations.

## 12. User Notice

Where appropriate and legally permitted, TorBox may notify a user that TorBox received an abuse report or took action regarding the user’s account or activity. TorBox is not required to provide notice if TorBox determines that notice would create legal, security, safety, privacy, abuse, enforcement, operational, or risk-management concerns.

## 13. Abuse of the Reporting Process

You must not submit false, misleading, abusive, fraudulent, duplicative, automated, harassing, or bad-faith reports.

TorBox may reject reports or restrict reporting access if TorBox believes the reporting process is being misused. Misuse of the reporting process may also violate the Terms of Service or Acceptable Use Policy.

## 14. No Legal Advice

This Policy is provided for informational and operational purposes and does not constitute legal advice. If you are unsure whether material or activity is illegal, violates your rights, or should be reported, you should consult an attorney or appropriate authority.

## 15. Changes to this Policy

TorBox may update this Policy from time to time. The updated Policy will be posted on or through the Service and will be effective as of the date stated in the updated Policy, unless a different effective date is required by law.

Your continued use of the Service after the updated Policy becomes effective means that you accept the updated Policy. If you do not agree to the updated Policy, you must stop using the Service.
